checks/audits/jobs--2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000-2026-10-03-r7-editor-page.txt:12:The Federal Reserve's two goals are maximum employment and price stability, and on September 16 it raised its target range for the federal funds rate by 1/4 percentage point. This is the last monthly jobs report before its committee meets on October 27-28; the next one, for October, is scheduled for November 6. On prices, the personal consumption expenditures price index for August was up 3.4 percent from a year earlier, and this report put average hourly earnings up 3.0 percent over the past 12 months.
