src/pages/events/jobs/2026-10-02-september-payrolls-rise-29000.astro:107:        <p data-layer="narrative" data-answer="3">USA Today headlined the release &ldquo;September jobs report shows slowdown in hiring, unemployment ticks up&rdquo;.<Cite s="usatoday-september-jobs" passage="September jobs report shows slowdown in hiring, unemployment ticks up" /> Neither half is a change the bureau itself reports: its summary says payrolls and the unemployment rate both &ldquo;changed little&rdquo;.<Cite s="bls-empsit-2026-09" passage="Both nonfarm payroll employment (+29,000) and the unemployment rate (4.2 percent) changed little in September" /> On hiring, the report does not count hires. Its {jobs(septemberPayrollChange * 1000)} is the net change in payroll jobs, and the bureau says a monthly change has to be about {jobs(establishment.significanceThreshold * 1000)} before it is statistically significant, that is, larger than the survey's margin of error.<Cite s="bls-empsit-2026-09" passage="An over-the-month employment change of about 122,000 is statistically significant in the establishment survey" /><Cite s="bls-empsit-2026-09" passage="The establishment survey employment series has a smaller margin of error on the measurement of month-to- month change than the household survey because of its much larger sample size." /> Hires, &ldquo;all additions to the payroll&rdquo; during the month, are counted in a separate survey, and September's count is scheduled for November 3.<Cite s="bls-jolts-2026-08" passage="all additions to the payroll" /><Cite s="bls-jolts-2026-08" passage="The Job Openings and Labor Turnover news release for September 2026 is scheduled to be published on Tuesday, November 3, 2026, at 10:00 a.m. (ET)." /></p>
